    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17124" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτμ-ίζω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤτμικα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					930b36
				</span></i>
			:—<i>smoke,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμὸς ἀτμίζων πυρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					370
				</span></i>
			; of water, <i>steam,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.5.15
			</span></i>: generally, <i>emit vapour,</i> of hot meat, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥδιστον ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					108.15
				</span></i>
			 codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπατμ-</span> edd.); of
			perspiration, interpol. post <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; of fresh-burnt tiles, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				383a24
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				388b32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be vaporized,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				349b23
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				358b16
			</span></i>,al.</div>
